{"availability":"available","full":"LemonFoxmere/DeepFusion","name":"DeepFusion","description":"A graphical approach to creating & training neural networks","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":18,"forks":1,"created":"2021-08-10T06:47:56Z","updated":"2026-03-23T23:09:28Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://lemonfoxmere.github.io/DeepFusion","topics":["canvas","deep-learning","gui","html-css-javascript","machine-learning","neural-networks","tensorflow","tensorflowjs","visualization","webapplication"],"demo":"https://lemonfoxmere.github.io/DeepFusion","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:17.333Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:17.333Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:17.333Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T21:05:17.333Z","stars":18,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["While there are apps out there that can create neural networks, or even more complex AI models, without the need for any code, none of them really satisfied my need for a simple, light weight, and easy to use app for making neural networks. Those which did satisfy those conditions, however, lacked many of the essential features needed in making and training neural networks. So I've decided to make one myself, and I think this is it.","But after all, this project isn't perfect, and I don't see it replace writing actual code in the near future, just like how scratch hasn't replaced javascript... yet. Plus, DeepFusion is still in its Beta stage, meaning that there's still a lot to be added. If YOU think this project isn't a terrible idea, you can suggest some features you would like to see here, and I'll most likely add it."],"features":["Navigating the Canvas","It has the ability to upload and train on custom data.","There are virtually no limitation to the size of the network.","You can train directly on the browser, although this is a double edge sword.","The program itself have infinite scalability for features."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LemonFoxmere/DeepFusion/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"057bc1510c46f919fa7a1d2ff681a44b2bf36a50f9a29c28d8e1795ab1908c60","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:17.539Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:17.539Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"While there are apps out there that can create neural networks, or even more complex AI models, without the need for any code, none of them really satisfied my need for a simple, light weight, and easy to use app for making neural networks. Those which did satisfy those conditions, however, lacked many of the essential features needed in making and training neural networks. So I've decided to make one myself, and I think this is it.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LemonFoxmere/DeepFusion/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"057bc1510c46f919fa7a1d2ff681a44b2bf36a50f9a29c28d8e1795ab1908c60","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LemonFoxmere/DeepFusion/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:17.539Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-03-23T23:09:28Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/LemonFoxmere/DeepFusion/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:17.540Z","hash":"057bc1510c46f919fa7a1d2ff681a44b2bf36a50f9a29c28d8e1795ab1908c60","originalBytes":13226,"storedBytes":13226,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["network","neural","button","deepfusion","node","layer","model","training","zoom","data","click","input","like","output","canvas","file","layers","project","there","train","upload","however","make","menu","name","need","connect","controls","dense","dock","export","just","least","license","may","must","one","see","test","tool","which","added","after","any","bottom","canvas.","code","contributing","easy","edit","feature","features","future","how","isn","it.","located","making","menu.","network.","networks","networks.","note","out","repo","scroll","shiel